ask-again = Press it again to take every key out of the settings file. The music folders and the files themselves are left alone.
put-back = Everything is back to what this build was made with.
this-build = The faces are the ones found on this machine when the window opened, and the reference is what the lookups reach this run.
places = The settings file is the one --config named, or the usual one where it named none; the catalog is the library every pane reads. Neither is moved from here.
updates = Asked at most once a day while the window is open, of the repository this build was released from. The question names this build and its version, nothing about you, and nothing is asked while Online is off.
nowhere-to-ask = This build names no repository it was released from, or was built without the online parts, so it never asks.
start-again = Puts every setting on this page and the others back to what this build starts with. The first press arms it and the second resets; the music folders, the catalog and the files are left alone.
